Overlay patch 0041: size screen-pass attachments from the ACQUIRED
drawable (= reference 0025, path retarget only; VISION-PRO-LUS-PLAYBOOK
Phase 01).
Vision Pro window-resize crash (reference device feedback #2):
SetupScreenFramebuffer receives the caller's cached width/height but binds
the freshly acquired drawable as the color attachment. During a live
resize the drawable's real size differs, so the depth texture (sized from
the stale values) mismatches the color attachment -> Metal render-pass
validation abort -> process restart while dragging the window corner. The
acquired drawable is ground truth — derive width/height from its texture.
Benign on iPhone (sizes never change there). Audit 2026-07-22: our fork's
anchor is verbatim (same src/fast/backends layout; the function is a class
method here, parameters identical); seven sibling patches touch
gfx_metal.cpp but none touch this anchor's context.

--- a/libultraship/src/fast/backends/gfx_metal.cpp
+++ b/libultraship/src/fast/backends/gfx_metal.cpp
@@ -1132,6 +1132,16 @@
     NS::AutoreleasePool* autorelease_pool = NS::AutoreleasePool::alloc()->init();
 
     tex.texture = mCurrentDrawable->texture();
+
+#ifdef __IOS__
+    // SOH_IOS (overlay 0041): during a live window resize (visionOS) the
+    // acquired drawable's size can differ from the caller's cached w/h;
+    // sizing the depth attachment from stale values makes the render pass
+    // attachments mismatch -> Metal validation abort. The drawable is the
+    // ground truth.
+    width = (uint32_t)tex.texture->width();
+    height = (uint32_t)tex.texture->height();
+#endif
 
     MTL::RenderPassDescriptor* render_pass_descriptor = MTL::RenderPassDescriptor::renderPassDescriptor();
     render_pass_descriptor->colorAttachments()->object(0)->setTexture(tex.texture);
